msgstr "ドアです。窓があるため、閉じていても視界を遮りません。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "carbon fiber sliding door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'recharging station'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A device for recharging batteries, capable of higher output than most "
"consumer models.  When turned on, it charges any rechargeable batteries "
"(battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc) placed directly in the attached "
"storage space."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'battery charger'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small, low-power consumer device for recharging batteries.  It slowly "
"charges any rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc)"
" placed directly in the attached storage space."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'stereo system'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A stereo system.  When turned on, it plays music, improving your mood."
msgstr "電源を入れるとステレオシステムが音楽を再生し、意欲が上昇します。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "chimes"
msgstr "チャイム"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'chimes'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A collection of electronic bells.  Use the vehicle's controls to turn it on "
"or off.  When turned on, it makes noise, attracting neighborhood children."
msgstr "車両制御装置を使って電源を入れると、オンオフを切り替えられます。オンにすると電子チャイムが音を鳴らし、近所の子供が集まってきます。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'jumper cable'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one vehicle "
"and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power between the "
"two."
msgstr "両端に鉛の部品が付いた、太い銅線です。一方の端を車両に接続し、もう一方の端を別の車両に接続すると、2台の車両間で電力を供給できます。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'heavy-duty cable'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Very thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one "
"vehicle and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power "
"between the two."
msgstr "両端に鉛の部品が付いた、非常に太い銅線です。一方の端を車両に接続し、もう一方の端を別の車両に接続すると、2台の車両間で電力を供給できます。"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty tow cable
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A heavy duty tow cable, if the other end was attached to another vehicle, it"
" could pull it."
msgstr "非常に重い牽引ケーブルです。ケーブルのもう一方端が他の車両に取り付けられていれば牽引できます。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden seat"
msgstr "座席(木)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden seat'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A place to sit."
msgstr "座る場所です。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "light wooden seat"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden spike"
msgstr "スパイク(木)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden spike'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A wooden spike, attached to the vehicle, to increase injury when crashing "
"into things."
msgstr "車両に衝突した物体に更にダメージを与える、車両に溶接したスパイクです。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden door"
msgstr "ドア(木)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "opaque wooden door"
msgstr "不透明ドア(木)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden roof"
msgstr "屋根(木)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden roof'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A wooden roof."
msgstr "木製のルーフです。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "chitin plating"
msgstr "装甲板(キチン)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "biosilicified chitin plating"
msgstr "装甲板(シリコンキチン)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "door motor"
msgstr "ドアモーター"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'door motor'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small electric motor.  Installed on the same frame as a door or curtain, "
"it will allow you to remotely open the door or curtain from the vehicle "
"controls."
msgstr ""
"小型の電動モーターです。ドアやカーテンと同一のフレームに取り付けてあり、車両制御装置を通して自動でドアやカーテンの操作ができるようになっています。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'drive by wire controls'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A sophisticated set of electronic controls that allow you to control the "
"vehicle from a vehicle remote while you are not in it.  You can 'e'xamine "
"the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control key (default "
"'^')."
msgstr ""
"車両に乗っていない状態でも遠隔から車両を制御できる、高性能な電子制御装置です。このタイルを調べる(e)か車両運転を開始する(^)ことで使用できます。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "camera control system"
msgstr "カメラ制御システム"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'camera control system'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An LCD display attached to one or more cameras.  When turned on, it lets you"
" see from the cameras, but drains power from the vehicle's batteries.  You "
"can 'e'xamine the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control "
"key (default '^')."
msgstr ""
"複数のカメラと接続できるLCDディスプレイです。電源を入れると車両のバッテリーの電力を消費して、カメラに映る映像を確認できます。このタイルを調べる(e)か車両運転を開始する(^)ことで使用できます。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'security camera'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small camera.  Will relay what it can see to a camera control station."
msgstr "小型のカメラです。カメラ制御システムを通して映像を中継します。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "robot controls"
msgstr "ロボット制御装置"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'robot controls'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of controls to allow a vehicle to drive itself, or you to drive it "
"remotely using a controller."
msgstr "車両の自動走行や遠隔操作を行うためのシステムです。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'clock'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A clock, so you know what time it is."
msgstr "現在時刻を確認できる時計です。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'leather funnel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'birchbark funnel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'makeshift funnel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'funnel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'metal funnel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A funnel that will collect rainwater into the tank beneath it."
msgstr "下部のタンクに雨水を集める漏斗です。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'tarp raincatcher'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An improvised raincatcher made using a tarpaulin, to collect rainwater into "
"the tank beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "scoop"
msgstr "清掃車用スコップ"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'scoop'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A scoop.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it"
" will scoop up any loose items that it travels over, putting them into the "
"vehicle's storage."
msgstr "車両制御装置を使うと、電源のオンオフを切り替えられます。オンにすると走行経路上のアイテムを掬い上げ、車内の積載スペースに保管します。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'water purifier'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A water purifier, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  You can use it to "
"purify water in a container or in the vehicle's tanks.  'e'xamine the tile "
"with the purifier to use it."
msgstr ""
"車両のバッテリーの電力によって駆動する浄水器です。車両に取り付けてあるタンクなどの容器に入った水を浄水できます。このタイルを調べる(e)ことで浄水器を使用できます。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'plow'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A plow.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it "
"will create a furrow in any dirt it travels over, making it suitable for "
"planting seeds.  It should be placed in front of any seed drills on the "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"車両制御装置を使うと、電源のオンオフを切り替えられます。耕耘爪をオンにすると、走行経路上のあらゆる土を種まきに適した畝に変えます。播種機よりも前方に設置すべき部品です。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'seed drill'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'advanced seed drill'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A seed drill.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  You can load "
"it with seeds by examining it.  When turned on, it will drop seeds as the "
"vehicle moves, or plant them in furrowed dirt.  It should be placed behind "
"any plows on the vehicle, and any wheels should be placed so they won't run "
"over the plants."
msgstr ""
"車両制御装置を使うと、電源のオンオフを切り替えられます。播種機をオンにすると、走行経路上の種まき可能な地面の上に植物の種を撒きます。耕耘爪よりも後方に設置すべき部品であり、車輪がまいた種の上を走って潰してしまわないよう設置場所には注意が必要です。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'reaper'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"on, it will cut down plants that it travels over.  It should be placed in "
"front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient operation.  It does not "
"include cargo space of its own so you need install a cargo space of some "
"kind elsewhere in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"車両制御装置を使うと、電源のオンオフを切り替えられます。自動刈取機をオンにすると、走行経路上の収穫可能な植物を刈り取ります。効率的に運用するなら、耕耘爪よりも前方に設置すべき部品です。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'advanced reaper'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"turned on, it will stop the vehicle unless it has a strong engine.  When on,"
" it will cut down plants and store them in the vehicle's cargo.  It should "
"be placed in front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient operation.  It "
"has internal cargo space for collecting the harvest."
msgstr ""
"車両制御装置を使うと、電源のオンオフを切り替えられます。改良型刈取機をオンにすると、走行経路上の収穫可能な植物を刈り取って車内の積載スペースに保管しますが、エンジンの性能が悪いと車両は停止してしまいます。効率的に運用するなら、耕耘爪よりも前方に設置すべき部品です。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "cargo lock"
msgstr "カーゴロック"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cargo lock'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of locks.  Attached to a suitable cargo space, it will prevent other "
"people from accessing the cargo and taking your stuff."
msgstr "この錠を対応する貨物スペースに取り付けておけば、他人に中の物資を奪われるのを予防できます。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'turret mount'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A rotating, universal mount for a weapon.  Weapons installed on it can be "
"fired from the vehicle controls.  If your hands are empty, you can also "
"stand on the same tile as a mounted gun and 'f'ire the weapon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "simple foldable wooden turret mount"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'simple foldable wooden turret mount'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A simple hardpoint for mounting a weapon.  Can only be fired manually, and "
"can't accept turret controls.  If your hands are empty, you can stand on the"
" same tile as a mounted gun and 'f'ire the weapon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "simple foldable light turret mount"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'simple foldable light turret mount'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'simple wooden turret mount'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'simple steel turret mount'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A simple hardpoint for mounting a weapon.  Lacks the necessary electronics "
"to support firing remotely or installing turret controls.  If your hands are"
" empty, you can stand on the same tile as a mounted gun and 'f'ire the "
"weapon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "simple wooden turret mount"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "simple steel turret mount"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "simple carbon fiber turret mount"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'turret control unit'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of motor, camera, and an AI unit which allows for tracking targets, "
"friend-or-foe identification, and firing the connected turret in full "
"automatic mode.  When installed over the turret, it will enable auto "
"targeting mode for said turret."
msgstr ""
"標的の追跡や敵味方の識別、全自動射撃などの機能が付いた、モーターやカメラ、AIユニットのセットです。タレットに取り付けると自動照準モードが有効になります。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "refrigerated tank (60L)"
msgstr "冷蔵タンク(60L)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'refrigerated tank (60L)'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A 60L refrigerated tank.  When turned on, it will cool the liquid inside, "
"extending the time until the food spoils."
msgstr "容量60Lの冷蔵タンクです。電源を入れると中に入れた液体が冷え、日持ちするようになります。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "mounted American flag"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mounted American flag'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "An American flag, fluttering in the breeze atop a vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "mounted Jolly Roger"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mounted Jolly Roger'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A black pirate flag, fluttering in the breeze atop a vehicle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'foldable solar panel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A foldable solar panel.  Will very slowly recharge the vehicle's electrical "
"power when exposed to the sun.  Clouds will slow the recharge speed even "
"more."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"An alternator.  When mounted on a gasoline or diesel engine and the engine "
"is on, will produce electrical power that can be stored in a battery."
msgstr "ガソリンまたはディーゼルエンジンに対応したオルタネーターです。エンジンが始動すると発電し、バッテリーに電力を蓄えます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "You can move through this vehicle frame without being slowed down."
msgstr "この車両フレーム上を移動しても速度は低下しません。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "A bright light that illuminates several squares inside the vehicle."
msgstr "車内の一区画を明るく照らします。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"Armor plate.  Will partially protect other components on the same frame from"
" damage from direct attacks but not from the shock damage of a distant "
"collision."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "You can sleep here comfortably."
msgstr "ここで快適に眠れます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"You can install a seat belt or five part harness here to help keep you in "
"your seat during a collision."
msgstr "ここにシートベルトや5点式シートベルトを取り付けると、衝突時に座席から投げ出されるのを防ぎます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "You can store items here."
msgstr "ここにアイテムを積載できます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"You can 'e'xamine the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle "
"control key (default '^')."
msgstr "このタイルを調べる(e)か車両運転を開始する(^)と車両の運転が可能になります。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"With a seat or saddle, you drive from here.  You can 'e'xamine the tile to "
"access the controls, or use the vehicle control key (default '^')."
msgstr "座席やサドルに座り、ここから車両を運転します。このタイルを調べる(e)か車両運転を開始する(^)と車両の運転が可能になります。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "Allows you to fire two-handed weapons while driving."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "Illuminated items in this space will not illuminate nearby squares."
msgstr "この区画内の照明アイテムは周囲を照らしません。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"Closed, it prevents people from seeing through the curtain.  A door motor "
"allows you to remotely open or close it from the vehicle controls."
msgstr "閉めるとカーテンによって視界を遮ります。ドアモーターがあれば、車両制御装置を使って自動で開閉できます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"When open, this part lets you move from inside the vehicle to outside or "
"vice versa.  When closed, it prevents people from entering or leaving the "
"vehicle."
msgstr "開けると車両への乗降が可能になり、閉じると乗降を妨げます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "When turned on, this device drains power from the vehicle's batteries."
msgstr "この装置の電源を入れると、車両のバッテリーの電力を消費します。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"Provides motive power to move the vehicle if the vehicle has sufficient "
"wheels.  Requires controls to turn on.  If it drains power, also requires a "
"charged battery to start."
msgstr "車輪が正常に取り付けられていれば、車両が走行します。制御装置をオンにする必要があります。電力が無い場合は、充電済みのバッテリーが必要です。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"An alternator can be attached, and it will generate electrical power while "
"the engine is on at the cost of some motive power."
msgstr "オルタネーターを取り付ければ、稼働中のエンジンの動力を利用して電力を生成します。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"When turned on, it will stop the vehicle unless it has a strong engine."
msgstr "電源がオンになっていると、エンジンが弱い車両は停止します。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"Each boat hull will reduce the draft of your vehicle and increase the height"
" sealed against water.  If the draft is less than the sealed height, your "
"vehicle will float if placed in water."
msgstr "各船体は車両の喫水線を下げ、防水位置を上げます。喫水線が防水位置より低ければ、車体が水面に浮かびます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"There's no place to attach a seat belt, so you get thrown from the vehicle "
"in a crash."
msgstr "シートベルトを取り付けられないため、衝突時に座席から投げ出される可能性があります。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "Keeps the rain out of the interior of the vehicle."
msgstr "車内を雨から守ります。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "You need to be in a seat or saddle to operate vehicle controls."
msgstr "車両制御装置を操作するには、座席かサドルが必要です。 "

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"This part will help prevent you from being thrown from the vehicle in a "
"collision.  You will automatically enable this part when you move into a "
"tile with it."
msgstr "この部品は、衝突時に車両から投げ出されるのを防ぎます。タイル上にいると自動で機能が有効化します。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"Armor plate.  Will partially protect other components on the same frame from"
" the shock damage of a distant collision but not from direct attacks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"If your vehicle consists of a single tile, this wheel is enough to allow it "
"to move."
msgstr "車両が1タイルのみで構成されている場合、このホイールで車両を移動できます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "Your vehicle needs at least one set of steerable wheels to turn."
msgstr "車両には少なくとも1組の転舵輪が必要です。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"A heavy weapon mounted in a turret.  If your hands are empty, you can stand "
"on the same tile as a mounted gun and 'f'ire the weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid ""
"If the center of balance of your vehicle is between all the wheels, the "
"vehicle will be able to move, provided it has an active engine or motor with"
" enough power to move the vehicle."
msgstr "全てのホイールの中心に車両の重心がある状態で、車両を動かすのに十分な性能をもつエンジンまたはモーターが起動していれば、車両は動きます。"

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "This item <good>can be used as a butchering rack</good>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Please leave anything in <angle brackets> unchanged.
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vp_flags.json
msgid "You can craft here."
msgstr "この場所でアイテム製作ができます。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "light wheel mount (steerable)"
msgstr "小型ホイールハブ (転舵輪)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "wheel hub assembly"
msgstr "ホイールハブ"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wheel hub assembly'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid ""
"Connection where wheels can be connected on.  This particular one is fit for"
" normal car wheels."
msgstr "ホイールを接続できる部品です。この車軸は通常の車両用ホイールに対応しています。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "wheel hub assembly (steerable)"
msgstr "ホイールハブ (転舵輪)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'heavy wheel hub assembly'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid ""
"Connection where wheels can be connected on.  This particular one is fit for"
" large car wheels."
msgstr "ホイールを接続できる部品です。この車軸は大型の車両用ホイールに対応しています。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "heavy wheel hub assembly (steerable)"
msgstr "大型ホイールハブ (転舵輪)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'rail wheel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid ""
"A strong metal wheel.  A flange helps keep it on a rail, but makes it "
"perform terribly when not on a rail."
msgstr "頑丈な金属製の車輪です。車輪縁の出っ張りのお陰でレール上を走り続けられますが、それ以外の場所での走行性は最悪です。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "rail wheel (steerable)"
msgstr "鉄道用ホイール(転舵輪)"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'pair of small rail wheels'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid ""
"A pair of small rail wheels.  It performs well when riding on a pair of "
"small rails.  It performs terribly when not on a rail.  Moreover, you can't "
"steer it."
msgstr "２つセットになった小型の鉄道用車輪です。普通の鉄道より狭いレール上を走れますが、操縦はできません。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "roller drum"
msgstr "ドラムローラー"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wheel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "A wheel."
msgstr "ホイールです。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "racing slick"
msgstr "スリックタイヤ"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'armored wheel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "A very strong, armored metal wheel."
msgstr "非常に頑丈な、装甲付きの金属製ホイールです。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wheelbarrow wheel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'small wheel'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'unicycle wheel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "A small wheel."
msgstr "小型のホイールです。"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'bicycle wheel'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "A thin bicycle wheel."
msgstr "幅の狭い自転車用ホイールです。"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid "casters"
msgstr "キャスター"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'casters'}
#: data/json/vehicleparts/wheel.json
msgid ""
